1
00:00:00,730 --> 00:00:05,770
Pie charts or pie graphs, I have
mixed feelings about. Some people

2
00:00:05,770 --> 00:00:10,370
love them, some people do not like
them. They are mostly effective

3
00:00:10,370 --> 00:00:14,090
if you have between three to five
categories that you're trying

4
00:00:14,090 --> 00:00:21,790
to display how much of the total
they take up. Now with pie charts

5
00:00:21,790 --> 00:00:26,490
especially, you need to be careful
because as much as we think we're

6
00:00:26,490 --> 00:00:31,230
great at interpreting angles,
which are what pie charts rely on.

7
00:00:31,670 --> 00:00:35,510
Unless there's one category that's
significantly greater than the other

8
00:00:35,510 --> 00:00:41,630
categories, a pie chart's not going
to be as easily interpreted as

9
00:00:41,630 --> 00:00:44,890
we may hope. We can do some things
to help with that. We can display

10
00:00:44,890 --> 00:00:49,470
the percentage that each category
is taking up, but I tend to stay

11
00:00:49,470 --> 00:00:54,780
away from a pie chart and tend to do
a column chart that's been changed

12
00:00:54,780 --> 00:01:00,430
to display 100% and then broken
down by that category just so that

13
00:01:00,430 --> 00:01:04,910
way it's a lot easier for your eye
to see. You're really, your eyes

14
00:01:04,910 --> 00:01:09,670
are a lot better at finding height
differences than angle differences.